    {
      "short": "Two numbers",
      "chapter": "setup",
      "title": "Fast and busy are different questions",
      "body": [
        "Stampwise runs an API that renders shipping labels. Two questions describe how it's doing: <span class=\"term\">latency</span> — how long does one request take? — and <span class=\"term\">throughput</span> — how many requests does it finish each second?",
        "Right now 40 requests arrive per second and each needs about 40 ms of work. The server can finish about 200 per second, so it is busy just 20% of the time. That fraction is its <span class=\"term\">utilization</span>."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "insight",
        "text": "A sports car is fast but carries two people; a bus is slow but carries fifty. Latency and throughput are separate dials."
      },
