      "short": "Percentiles",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "title": "Averages hide the slow ones",
      "body": [
        "Latency isn't one number. Sort a minute of requests by duration: the one in the middle is the <span class=\"term\">p50</span> (median); the one slower than 99% of the others is the <span class=\"term\">p99</span>.",
        "Here p50 is 42 ms but p99 is 110 ms — a few requests hit a cold cache, a garbage-collection pause or a slow disk. The average, about 50 ms, describes nobody in particular."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Watch p50 for the typical experience and p95/p99 for the unlucky. Your most active users send the most requests, so they meet the tail most often."
      },
