    {
      "short": "Fan-out",
      "chapter": "problem",
      "title": "When one page waits on many calls",
      "body": [
        "Stampwise's dashboard page calls five internal services in parallel and can render only when <i>all</i> of them have answered. The page is as slow as its slowest call.",
        "If each call has a 1% chance of a p99-slow reply, the chance at least one of five is slow is 1 − 0.99⁵ ≈ <b>5%</b>. With 20 calls it's ≈ <b>18%</b>. This <span class=\"term\">tail amplification</span> turns a backend's rare case into a common one."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "insight",
        "text": "The more calls a request fans out to, the more the <b>tail</b> of each one matters."
      },
      "changes": [
        "+ Five backend services",
        "~ Page waits for the slowest answer"
      ],
