      "title": "Fast vs busy, in five lines",
      "body": [
        "<ul class=\"takeaways\"><li><b>Latency</b> is time per request; <b>throughput</b> is requests finished per second.</li><li>Report percentiles: p50 for the typical case, p99 for the tail — and fan-out makes the tail common.</li><li>Waiting grows like ρ ÷ (1 − ρ): gentle at first, explosive near saturation.</li><li>Past capacity, throughput flatlines and queues grow without limit.</li><li>Keep headroom: aim for the knee of the curve, not 100%.</li></ul>"
